# Hits that are correct to keep: rule-id file symbol reason. An entry with no reason, or matching nothing, fails the check.
# Show whose text is the type's meaning: derived output would change what is displayed or stored.
hand-instance apps/dashboard/src/Dashboard/Route.purs instance-Show-Route the text is the route's URL (print route)
hand-instance packages/world/src/World/Error.purs instance-Show-ValidationError the text is the user-facing validation message
hand-instance packages/world/src/World/Error.purs instance-Show-Inconsistency the text is the user-facing message
hand-instance packages/checks/src/Checks/Round.purs instance-Show-Field the text is the prose an assertion failure reports
hand-instance packages/checks/src/Checks/Round.purs instance-Show-Failure the text is the prose an assertion failure reports
hand-instance packages/laws/src/Laws/Engine/Commit.purs instance-Show-EngineError the text is the engine's error message
hand-instance packages/laws/src/Laws/Invariants.purs instance-Show-Invariant the text is the spec's id (INV-01), which a constructor cannot spell
hand-instance packages/core/src/Core/Num.purs instance-Show-Q the text is the exact decimal form (Q.format)
hand-instance packages/schema/src/Schema/Run.purs instance-Show-RunStatus the text is the status as stored
hand-instance packages/schema/src/Schema/Run.purs instance-Show-DeriveKind the text is the kind as stored
hand-instance packages/core/src/Core/Shape.purs instance-Show-TagForm the text is the prose name a prompt shows
hand-instance packages/core/src/Core/Types.purs instance-Show-Id the text is the id itself, used wherever an id is displayed
hand-instance packages/laws/src/Laws/Types.purs instance-Show-RefKind the text is the lower-case name error messages use
hand-instance packages/assembly/src/Assembly/Error.purs instance-Show-AssemblyError the text is the user-facing message (renderAssemblyError)
hand-instance packages/schema/src/Schema/PossibleWorld.purs instance-Show-Outcome the text is the outcome as a view shows it (not met)
# JSON handled as JSON, not a payload with a type behind it.
hand-json apps/cli/src/Render.purs sortKeys canonicalises any compiled JSON; no type is being encoded
hand-json packages/premises/src/Premises/Load.purs merge merges premise files as JSON objects before decoding
hand-json packages/premises/src/Premises/Compose.purs files splits a compiled document into its premise files by key
# Not renames: each fixes a type or names a DSL word.
alias packages/core/src/Core/Map.purs entries fixes the polymorphic toUnfoldable to Array; it is the helper repeated-idiom points to
alias packages/schema/src/Schema/Build/World.purs atLeast DSL word for a lower bound; premises read better for it
# The engine's own reading of Events.
silent-default packages/laws/src/Laws/Engine/Commit.purs prepared engine code: the engine's own reading of the Events it produced
# One rule per Intent kind, not a walk of its references.
intent-walk packages/laws/src/Laws/Authority.purs authorized the authority rule differs per kind; there is nothing to traverse
# Format-pinning tests are not built with the thing they test.
test-literal packages/schema/test/Main.purs main format-pinning test: JSON text in schema decode tests
implicit-codec packages/laws/test/Main.purs roundTrip format-pinning test: pins the argonaut instance's round trip
implicit-codec packages/laws/test/Main.purs main format-pinning test: pins the wire form of an Intent
implicit-codec packages/handlers/test/Test/Handlers/SimCapstone.purs spec format-pinning test: byte identity between the shape and the instance
implicit-codec packages/adapters/test/Main.purs main format-pinning test: byte identity of records through the store
implicit-codec packages/adapters/test/Test/Adapters/Capstone.purs spec format-pinning test: byte identity of records and snapshots through the store
implicit-codec packages/handlers/test/Main.purs main format-pinning test: byte identity of recorded inputs
implicit-codec packages/premises/test/Main.purs main format-pinning test: deliberately malformed premise files
intent-walk packages/laws/src/Laws/Types.purs jointIntent which Intents a joint CandidateTransaction may bundle; a per-kind rule, nothing to traverse
# Guarded or merged constructors of a premise sum: not a one-to-one image of the type's constructors (S6).
sum-projection packages/schema/src/Schema/Premise/Intent.purs intentShape a trade and a route share one premise form, and enact and repeal are separate tags over ChangeRule
sum-projection packages/schema/src/Schema/Premise/StrategyRules.purs templateShape a joint CandidateTransaction and a Procedure share one Template constructor, split by their procedure and shape
test-literal packages/strategy/test/Main.purs main format-pinning test: a nested Procedure in StrategyRules JSON must not decode
name-literal packages/handlers/src/Handlers/SqlStore.purs roundsTable a table name of the store, not the specification key that spells the same word
# Each line names why this one hit is correct to keep; the rule's fix text applies everywhere else.
hand-instance packages/laws/src/Laws/World.purs instance-Show-RejectReason the text is the rejection's display text (renderReason), the one place it is written
hand-json apps/dashboard/src/Dashboard/Chart.purs chartRows a chart row's keys are the series names, known only at run time; no shape can name them
hand-json apps/dashboard/src/Dashboard/Chart.purs barRows a chart row's keys are the series names, known only at run time; no shape can name them
hand-json apps/dashboard/src/Dashboard/Components.purs stackedBars a bar row's keys are the action kinds, known only at run time; no shape can name them
name-literal apps/dashboard/src/Dashboard/Launch.purs emptyForm the launch form's own default preset (docs/06 §9.1), not a copy of a list: it is checked against GET /api/premise's presets
name-literal packages/schema/src/Schema/Premise/Fixture.purs procedureShape the name of this record's shape, in which an Event kind's name is reused as an English word
implicit-codec apps/server/test/Main.purs main format-pinning test: request and reply JSON are the wire format of docs/06 §8.1
implicit-codec packages/adapters/test/Test/Adapters/Pi.purs streamOf format-pinning test: the raw pi event stream of docs/06 §5
intent-walk packages/handlers/test/Test/Handlers/Shock.purs roundKinds the test's own label per kind of Intent; a label is not a walk of an Intent's references
intent-walk packages/strategy/src/Strategy/Interpret.purs zeroQuantity one rule per kind of Intent (a ChangeRule has no quantity), not a walk of its references
alias packages/views/src/Views/Common.purs quantity a cell's display kind by name: every view cell names its kind (docs/02 §9.1)
alias packages/views/src/Views/Common.purs price a cell's display kind by name: every view cell names its kind (docs/02 §9.1)
alias packages/views/src/Views/Common.purs ratio a cell's display kind by name: every view cell names its kind (docs/02 §9.1)
alias packages/views/src/Views/Common.purs exact a chart value is sent exactly, and the name states that a cell is not a display value
intent-walk packages/views/src/Views/BalanceSheet.purs intentText a player-facing sentence per kind of Intent; a label is not a walk of the Intent
name-literal packages/views/src/Views/BalanceSheet.purs doneTable the balance sheet's own column headings, for a player and not a glossary name
name-literal packages/views/src/Views/BalanceSheet.purs exchangeTable the balance sheet's own column headings, for a player and not a glossary name
name-literal packages/views/src/Views/BalanceSheet.purs transformationTable the balance sheet's own column headings, for a player and not a glossary name
hand-json apps/server/src/Server/OpenApi.purs obj an OpenAPI document is itself the output of the Shape interpreters, in a format no type here decodes
